:","options":["Herbivores","Producers","Carnivores","Decomposers"],"correctIndex":2,"page":22,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Carnivores."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-34a0036e3289ab60","chapterId":"el-b52-c2","topicId":"el-b52-t2707-0","type":"mcq","text":"Organisms that break down dead plants and animals are called:","options":["Producers","Herbivores","Carnivores","Decomposers"],"correctIndex":3,"page":22,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"e.g. bacteria and fungi."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-146b34f87de224d9","chapterId":"el-b52-c2","topicId":"el-b52-t2707-0","type":"mcq","text":"Which is a correct food chain?","options":["Fox → Grass → Rabbit","Rabbit → Grass → Fox","Grass → Fox → Rabbit","Grass → Rabbit → Fox"],"correctIndex":3,"page":22,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Energy flows from producer."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-1a82423343ea1479","chapterId":"el-b52-c2","topicId":"el-b52-t2707-0","type":"mcq","text":"The natural home of an organism is called its:","options":["Habitat","Food","Population","Shelter only"],"correctIndex":0,"page":22,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Habitat."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-f37a7d6053d1c6e4","chapterId":"el-b52-c2","topicId":"el-b52-t2707-0","type":"mcq","text":"Animals that eat both plants and animals are called:","options":["Herbivores","Carnivores","Omnivores","Producers"],"correctIndex":2,"page":22,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Omnivores."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-14a7482b388c763c","chapterId":"el-b52-c2","topicId":"el-b52-t2707-0","type":"mcq","text":"The main source of energy for all ecosystems is the:","options":["Moon","Soil","Water","Sun"],"correctIndex":3,"page":22,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Sunlight."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-77c070ba1dd32f74","chapterId":"el-b52-c2","topicId":"el-b52-t2707-0","type":"mcq","text":"A camel is adapted to live in the:","options":["Ocean","Polar region","Rainforest","Desert"],"correctIndex":3,"page":22,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Stores fat and water."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-6fca3db63e6f5daf","chapterId":"el-b52-c2","topicId":"el-b52-t2707-0","type":"mcq","text":"An animal that hunts other animals is called a:","options":["Prey","Producer","Predator","Decomposer"],"correctIndex":2,"page":22,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Predator."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-bd205f947afad73c","chapterId":"el-b52-c3","topicId":"el-b52-t2715-0","type":"mcq","text":"A balanced diet contains:","options":["Only proteins","Only fats","Only sweets","All nutrients in correct amounts"],"correctIndex":3,"page":34,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Balanced diet."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-ee4fc57bc8b90c0d","chapterId":"el-b52-c3","topicId":"el-b52-t2715-0","type":"mcq","text":"Carbohydrates give us:","options":["Strong bones only","Vitamins","Water","Energy"],"correctIndex":3,"page":34,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Energy-giving food."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-c8a3c99fa4d2113b","chapterId":"el-b52-c3","topicId":"el-b52-t2715-0","type":"mcq","text":"Proteins are needed for:","options":["Growth and repair of the body","Only energy","Only water","Colour"],"correctIndex":0,"page":34,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Body-building food."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-c149fe5ada9c0c15","chapterId":"el-b52-c3","topicId":"el-b52-t2715-0","type":"mcq","text":"Lack of Vitamin C causes:","options":["Rickets","Scurvy","Night blindness","Goitre"],"correctIndex":1,"page":34,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Vitamin C deficiency."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-d649d126e43ac2ee","chapterId":"el-b52-c3","topicId":"el-b52-t2715-0","type":"mcq","text":"Milk is a good source of:","options":["Iron only","Fibre","Calcium","Starch only"],"correctIndex":2,"page":34,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Strong bones and teeth."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-2d421d45e8cd0f96","chapterId":"el-b52-c3","topicId":"el-b52-t2715-0","type":"mcq","text":"We should wash our hands before:","options":["Sleeping","Reading","Eating","Walking"],"correctIndex":2,"page":34,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Hygiene."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-9f48dbdd39083109","chapterId":"el-b52-c3","topicId":"el-b52-t2715-0","type":"mcq","text":"Diseases that spread from one person to another are called:","options":["Deficiency diseases","Genetic diseases","Communicable diseases","Allergies"],"correctIndex":2,"page":34,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Infectious diseases."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-601cf10227a83a6a","chapterId":"el-b52-c3","topicId":"el-b52-t2715-0","type":"mcq","text":"Lack of iron in the diet causes:","options":["Scurvy","Rickets","Goitre","Anaemia"],"correctIndex":3,"page":34,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Iron deficiency."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-5335efbcdc444b07","chapterId":"el-b52-c3","topicId":"el-b52-t2715-0","type":"mcq","text":"We should brush our teeth at least:","options":["Once a week","Twice a day","Once a month","Never"],"correctIndex":1,"page":34,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Dental hygiene."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-492651efd945e672","chapterId":"el-b52-c3","topicId":"el-b52-t2715-0","type":"mcq","text":"Fruits and vegetables are rich in:","options":["Fats only","Proteins only","Vitamins and minerals","Sugar only"],"correctIndex":2,"page":34,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Protective foods."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-3bf16b67324ca3b7","chapterId":"el-b52-c4","topicId":"el-b52-t2721-0","type":"mcq","text":"Anything that has mass and occupies space is called:","options":["Matter","Energy","Force","Light"],"correctIndex":0,"page":46,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Matter."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-7997ca45de6d621d","chapterId":"el-b52-c4","topicId":"el-b52-t2721-0","type":"mcq","text":"The three states of matter are:","options":["Hot, cold and warm","Solid, liquid and gas","Hard, soft and rough","Water, ice and stone"],"correctIndex":1,"page":46,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"States of 