ng point at sea level."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-c09a40aaa2249f57","chapterId":"el-b52-c4","topicId":"el-b52-t2721-0","type":"mcq","text":"Air is an example of a:","options":["Solid","Gas","Liquid","Metal"],"correctIndex":1,"page":46,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Air is a gas."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-fdb60825697a8ecf","chapterId":"el-b52-c5","topicId":"el-b52-t2726-0","type":"mcq","text":"Energy cannot be created or:","options":["Used","Changed","Destroyed","Measured"],"correctIndex":2,"page":58,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Conservation of energy."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-d17a4702f37ea55a","chapterId":"el-b52-c5","topicId":"el-b52-t2726-0","type":"mcq","text":"Heat moves from a hotter object to a:","options":["Hotter object","Heavier object","Colder object","Bigger object"],"correctIndex":2,"page":58,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Heat transfer."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-fda211c7e2abd518","chapterId":"el-b52-c5","topicId":"el-b52-t2726-0","type":"mcq","text":"Transfer of heat through solids is called:","options":["Convection","Radiation","Evaporation","Conduction"],"correctIndex":3,"page":58,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Conduction."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-393fc67a044a439c","chapterId":"el-b52-c5","topicId":"el-b52-t2726-0","type":"mcq","text":"Heat from the Sun reaches the Earth by:","options":["Conduction","Convection","Evaporation","Radiation"],"correctIndex":3,"page":58,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"No medium needed."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-6c195ce6a9f2edf8","chapterId":"el-b52-c5","topicId":"el-b52-t2726-0","type":"mcq","text":"Metals are good:","options":["Insulators of heat","Conductors of heat","Producers","Absorbers of sound only"],"correctIndex":1,"page":58,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Metals conduct heat."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-4a459505f9cfb303","chapterId":"el-b52-c5","topicId":"el-b52-t2726-0","type":"mcq","text":"Wood and plastic are good:","options":["Conductors","Insulators","Magnets","Mirrors"],"correctIndex":1,"page":58,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"They do not conduct heat well."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-f3d7b93b8da2bfd2","chapterId":"el-b52-c5","topicId":"el-b52-t2726-0","type":"mcq","text":"A battery stores energy in the form of:","options":["Chemical energy","Heat energy","Sound energy","Light energy"],"correctIndex":0,"page":58,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Chemical energy."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-c0c668b9ac8bd1d9","chapterId":"el-b52-c5","topicId":"el-b52-t2726-0","type":"mcq","text":"A moving car has:","options":["Only potential energy","No energy","Kinetic energy","Sound energy only"],"correctIndex":2,"page":58,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Energy of motion."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-ea7dd276955811ed","chapterId":"el-b52-c5","topicId":"el-b52-t2726-0","type":"mcq","text":"Transfer of heat in liquids and gases by movement is called:","options":["Convection","Conduction","Radiation","Reflection"],"correctIndex":0,"page":58,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Convection."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-06cb60edbf0940b4","chapterId":"el-b52-c5","topicId":"el-b52-t2726-0","type":"mcq","text":"An electric bulb changes electrical energy into:","options":["Sound energy","Chemical energy","Kinetic energy","Light and heat energy"],"correctIndex":3,"page":58,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Energy change."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-8c572f352b0ee300","chapterId":"el-b52-c6","topicId":"el-b52-t2728-0","type":"mcq","text":"A push or a pull is called:","options":["Energy","Work","Force","Speed"],"correctIndex":2,"page":69,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Force."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-abde45ada5614fac","chapterId":"el-b52-c6","topicId":"el-b52-t2728-0","type":"mcq","text":"The force that pulls objects towards the Earth is:","options":["Gravity","Friction","Magnetism","Tension"],"correctIndex":0,"page":69,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Gravity."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-d32