ke poles attract."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-bb1cd8589c6e5954","chapterId":"el-b52-c6","topicId":"el-b52-t2728-0","type":"mcq","text":"Change in position of an object with time is called:","options":["Rest","Motion","Force","Energy"],"correctIndex":1,"page":69,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Motion."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-23d5a4cc408b7d1e","chapterId":"el-b52-c7","topicId":"el-b52-t2733-0","type":"mcq","text":"The outermost layer of the Earth is called the:","options":["Crust","Mantle","Core","Atmosphere"],"correctIndex":0,"page":83,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Crust."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-943c3a49d1e16831","chapterId":"el-b52-c7","topicId":"el-b52-t2733-0","type":"mcq","text":"Natural resources that can be replaced are called:","options":["Non-renewable resources","Renewable resources","Fossil fuels","Minerals"],"correctIndex":1,"page":83,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"e.g. sunlight, wind."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-0c603e8e2367ff2c","chapterId":"el-b52-c7","topicId":"el-b52-t2733-0","type":"mcq","text":"Coal, oil and gas are called:","options":["Renewable resources","Metals","Rocks only","Fossil fuels"],"correctIndex":3,"page":83,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Formed from dead organisms."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-0463ab8e46f65327","chapterId":"el-b52-c7","topicId":"el-b52-t2733-0","type":"mcq","text":"Which is a renewable resource?","options":["Wind","Coal","Petrol","Natural gas"],"correctIndex":0,"page":83,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Wind does not run out."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-5998dc6bb37fc985","chapterId":"el-b52-c7","topicId":"el-b52-t2733-0","type":"mcq","text":"Soil is formed by the breaking down of:","options":["Water","Rocks","Air","Plastic"],"correctIndex":1,"page":83,"difficulty":2,"source":"extra","explanation":"Weathering."},{"id":"el-b52-xelq-3aad2f1cc18d3b01","chapterId":"el-b52-c7","topicId":"el-b52-t2733-0","type":"mcq","text":"We should save water because it is:","options":["Unlimited"